<p class="hk-body">Ines Vermeulen founded the Hakari food-safety school in 2016 after fourteen years auditing hotel kitchens, school catering operations, and commercial food production facilities. Her teaching focuses on bridging the gap between rigorous hygiene regulations and the real-world pressure of a busy prep shift. Having assessed hundreds of service kitchens, Ines designed the core curriculum to give supervisors clear, repeatable verification routines rather than abstract paperwork. She leads the live Tuesday Q&amp;A sessions from our studio teaching kitchen at Havenkade 14 in Rotterdam, mentoring learners through complex HACCP queries and inspection management with calm, practical guidance.</p>
