<p class="hk-body">Samuel Adeyemi brings extensive commercial kitchen experience to his role as chef-trainer, specializing in thermal processing, cooking, rapid cooling, and safe reheating. Having led high-volume kitchen brigades, Samuel understands the commercial temptation to cut corners during peak service hours. He teaches supervisors how to build effortless temperature routines that protect guests without interrupting ticket times. In his lessons, Samuel breaks down core temperature checks to 75 °C, chilling protocols to 5 °C or below, and correct probe insertion techniques for diverse proteins and starches. He directly reviews practical cooling logs and provides detailed feedback on temperature control routines.</p>
